cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyunbil (동현빌): an educational village-outbreak laboratory on a real contact network, controlled through the esoteric language Donghyun-lang"
type: software
version: "0.38"
date-released: "2026-10-27"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab3"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab3/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyunbil is a browser-based, noncommercial educational laboratory for
  exploring infectious disease transmission, vaccination and isolation
  policies. It simulates hypothetical outbreaks (measles, pertussis,
  influenza) on the publicly released Haslemere contact data (469
  participants, 3 days, 5-minute resolution), with all interventions
  specified only through the esoteric programming language Donghyun-lang.
  Contacts are real; outbreaks are hypothetical. It is a teaching model, not a
  forecasting or policy-decision tool. The MIT license applies only to the
  original application code, documentation and artwork; no additional license
  is claimed over the Haslemere dataset, which is included unchanged with
  attribution to its authors, and the fonts are under the SIL Open Font
  License. See LICENSE, CREDITS.md and PROVENANCE.md.
keywords:
  - epidemiology education
  - infectious disease modelling
  - vaccination
  - contact network
  - citizen science data
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
